      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Consider the following false statement.\n\n${n}^{2}-6n+8\\ge 0$ for any $n\\in N.$\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that \n\n$$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀n\\in Z,\\,{n}^{2}-6n+8\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true. \n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true. \n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n¬(∀n\\in Z,\\,{n}^{2}-6n+8\\ge 0)\\,≡\\,∃n\\in Z,\\,{n}^{2}-6n+8<0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that \n\n$$\n{n}^{2}-6n+8<0.\n$$",
